---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';

/* Short on purpose. This site sells nothing, hosts no accounts and takes no
   submissions, so most of what a terms page normally governs does not exist
   here. Padding it out with clauses about services we do not run would make
   it less true, not more protective. */

const revised = '20 September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use for this site | Artemis Esports"
  description="The terms for using the Artemis Esports website: what is published here, what you may do with it, and what it does not promise."
  cta="none"
>
  <PageHead
    title="Terms"
    lead="What is published here, what you may do with it, and what it does not promise."
    meta={`Last revised ${revised}`}
  />

  <section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="site-heading">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2 class="display-md" id="site-heading">What this site is</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        A published record of an iRacing team: results, the roster, the
        calendar and how to join. There is nothing to buy here, nothing to
        sign up for, and no account to hold. Reading it costs you nothing and
        commits you to nothing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="use-heading">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2 class="display-md" id="use-heading">Using what is here</h2>
      <p>
        Quote us, link to us, screenshot a result, put a finishing position in
        a league write-up. That is what publishing it is for, and no
        permission is needed.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Artemis name, the wordmark, the notched A and the hero mark are
        ours, and passing yourself off as the team or implying a partnership
        that does not exist is the line. If you want to use the marks for
        something, ask.
      </p>
      <p>
        Driver names, liveries and photographs belong to the people and
        parties they came from. Car models, track names and series names
        belong to their own owners, and their appearance here is description,
        not a claim.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="accuracy-heading">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2 class="display-md" id="accuracy-heading">What it does not promise</h2>
      <p>
        Results, ratings and the calendar are published in good faith from
        what the team and iRacing report, and they can be wrong, stale, or
        briefly missing while something is being fixed. Nothing here is a
        guarantee of a seat, a result, or that a scheduled race will happen.
        If a number matters to you, check it against the league's own record.
      </p>
      <p>
        Open seats are described as honestly as we can manage, and applying is
        not an offer. The site can go down, and we do not promise it will be
        available at any given moment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="elsewhere-heading">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2 class="display-md" id="elsewhere-heading">Off this site</h2>
      <p>
        Links to Discord, the social channels and the store leave this site.
        We do not control them and these terms stop at the edge. The Discord
        has its own rules and Discord's terms apply there; the store is
        operated by someone else and their terms cover anything you buy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="changes-heading">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2 class="display-md" id="changes-heading">Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        These terms change when the site does, and the revision date above
        moves with them. There is no notification list, because there is no
        list.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>
        {site.contactEmail}
        <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} />
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .prose > * + * {
    margin-top: var(--space-m);
  }

  .prose p {
    color: var(--mist-dim);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
</style>
